{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">The model</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/interactions</code> is experimental helper sugar for client-triggered regions. Each helper accepts either a simple endpoint string or a configured interaction value. The connector turns that interaction into protocol attributes, and the interaction stage owns the final HTML wrapper.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">helper call -&gt; connector.Interaction -&gt; connector attributes -&gt; exp/interactions stage HTML</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Helpers</h2>
    <table class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800/90 text-left">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900"><tr><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Helper</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Intent</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">async</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Load after the page shell renders.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ async runtime \"/stats\" }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">reveal</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Load when the placeholder enters the viewport.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ reveal runtime \"/charts/monthly\" }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">poll</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Refresh on an interval.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ poll runtime Notifications }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">on</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Refresh when a named browser event is dispatched.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ on runtime CartChanged }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">stream</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Declare an SSE-backed region.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ stream runtime ActivityStream }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">prefetch</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Emit a non-visual prefetch hint.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ prefetch runtime \"/users/42\" }}" }}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">refresh</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Render a refresh control for a target.</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ refresh runtime CartRefresh }}" }}</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Two forms</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use a string endpoint when defaults are enough. Use a named go-clue contract when the interaction needs IDs, targets, intervals, placeholders, route params, or swap behavior.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">{{ "{{ async runtime \"/stats\" }}" }}</code></pre>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">{{ "{{/*" }}
@interaction Notifications github.com/donseba/go-partial/exp/interactions.Interaction
@interaction CartChanged github.com/donseba/go-partial/exp/interactions.Interaction
@interaction CartRefresh github.com/donseba/go-partial/exp/interactions.Interaction
{{ "*/}}" }}

{{ "{{ poll runtime Notifications }}" }}
{{ "{{ on runtime CartChanged }}" }}
{{ "{{ refresh runtime CartRefresh }}" }}</code></pre>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">content.SetContract("interaction",
    interactions.NewPoll("/notifications").As("Notifications").Every(10 * time.Second),
    interactions.NewOn("cart:changed", "/cart/summary").As("CartChanged").Target("#cart").Placeholder(""),
    interactions.NewRefresh("/cart/summary").As("CartRefresh").Target("#cart").Swap(interactions.SwapOuterHTML),
)</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Generic contracts</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Interaction roots use the same contract path as every other go-clue annotation. The interaction builder implements <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ContractName()</code>, so <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetContract</code> can bind it by name.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">content.SetContract("component", primaryButton)</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Route parameters</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Route parameters can be configured in Go with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Param</code>. The simple template form still accepts key/value pairs for route placeholders when that reads better in a loop.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">loader := interactions.NewAsync("/table/row/:row").Param("row", row.ID)</code></pre>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">{{ "{{ async runtime RowLoader }}" }}
{{ "{{ async runtime \"/table/row/:row\" \"row\" .Row.ID }}" }}</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Custom markup</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The default stage is intentionally simple. Applications can replace it when registering the optional interaction helper functions. The connector still supplies the protocol attributes, so your stage owns the element, classes, loading state, and accessibility text.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.Use(interactions.Stage(func(
    runtime *partial.Runtime,
    interaction connector.Interaction,
    attrs map[string]string,
) (template.HTML, error) {
    return template.HTML(renderMyWrapper(interaction, attrs)), nil
}))</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">HTMX output</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With the HTMX connector, helpers map to normal HTMX attributes. Polling defaults to <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">innerHTML</code> so the wrapper keeps its polling attributes after each response.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;div id="poll-notifications"
     hx-get="/notifications"
     hx-trigger="every 10s"
     hx-target="#poll-notifications"
     hx-swap="innerHTML"&gt;
    Loading...
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Reveal and infinite scroll</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">reveal</code> is the primitive behind infinite scroll. Render a sentinel near the bottom of a list, load the next page when it is revealed, and return a chunk that includes the next sentinel.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Attributes on your own elements</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">asyncAttrs</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">revealAttrs</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">pollAttrs</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">onAttrs</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">streamAttrs</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">refreshAttrs</code> return only the connector attributes, for an element the template already has, also conditionally. Without a target or id the interaction targets that element. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">interactions.AttrsFuncMap()</code> holds only these attribute helpers, for applications that keep generic names such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">poll</code> or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">on</code> for functions of their own.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;ul id="jobs"{{ "{{ if .Running }}" }}{{ "{{ pollAttrs runtime \"/jobs\" \"3s\" }}" }}{{ "{{ end }}" }}&gt;
&lt;tr {{ "{{ revealAttrs runtime \"/rows\" \"page\" .Next \"swap\" \"afterend\" }}" }}&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">"select"</code> picks the part of the response to swap (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-select</code> for htmx), and options whose names start with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">up-</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-</code> or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">aria-</code> are written on the element as given, replacing the connector's attribute of the same name.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;div {{ "{{ pollAttrs runtime \"/inbox\" \"every\" \"10s\" \"select\" \"#messages\" \"hx-indicator\" \"#spinner\" }}" }}&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Forms and live search</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">submitAttrs</code> makes a form post with the client library and swap the response into its target; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">liveAttrs</code> requests as the user types. The neutral options <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">include</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">pushURL</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">replaceURL</code> become <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-include</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-push-url</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-replace-url</code> with htmx; interaction values set them with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Option</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;form method="post" action="{{ "{{ .Action }}" }}" {{ "{{ submitAttrs runtime .Action \"target\" \"#comments\" \"swap\" \"outerHTML\" }}" }}&gt;
&lt;input type="search" name="q" {{ "{{ liveAttrs runtime \"/search\" \"target\" \"#content\" \"include\" \"closest form\" \"pushURL\" \"true\" }}" }}&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Link and form attributes</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientAttrs</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">noBoost</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">confirmAttr</code> write how the client library treats a link or form, in the connector's syntax: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-boost="false"</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-confirm</code> with htmx, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-turbo="false"</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-turbo-confirm</code> with Turbo, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">up-follow="false" up-submit="false"</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">up-confirm</code> with Unpoly. On the body, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientAttrs</code> also writes the settings of a whole page; see <a href="{{ basePath }}/connectors" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/connectors" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">Connectors</a>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;a href="/download.zip" {{ "{{ noBoost runtime }}" }}&gt;Download&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;button {{ "{{ confirmAttr runtime \"Delete this page?\" }}" }}&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;a href="/logout" {{ "{{ clientAttrs runtime \"confirm\" \"Log out?\" \"boost\" \"off\" }}" }}&gt;Log out&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Browser client</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The browser client of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/interactions</code> is a small script, with no build step and no other library, served from <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clients.FS()</code>, for what client libraries cannot do themselves. A submit button with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientAttrs runtime "submitConfirm" "Delete for good?"</code> asks its question before it sends its form. A link or form with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientAttrs runtime "reloadOnError" "true"</code>, or inside an element with it, whose request gets a 5xx status or no answer loads as a whole page: a link is followed and a GET form submitted again. A POST, PUT, PATCH or DELETE is never sent twice: the HTML error page the server answered replaces the page; without one the page stays and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:reload-on-error:failed</code> is dispatched on the link or form.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">mux.Handle("GET /assets/", http.StripPrefix("/assets/", http.FileServerFS(clients.FS())))

&lt;script src="/assets/partial-interactions.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clients.FS()</code> holds the client as the file <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial-interactions.js</code>, with the clients of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/flash</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/sse</code>, for applications that fingerprint their assets.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Confirmation dialog</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;dialog data-partial-confirm-dialog&gt;</code> in the page, the client asks the questions of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">"submitConfirm"</code> buttons and htmx's <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-confirm</code> (htmx 2 and 4) in that dialog instead of with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">window.confirm</code>, which some embedded browsers never show. The question goes into the element with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-confirm-question</code>; a button with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">value="confirm"</code> answers yes, and Escape or another button no. Without the dialog nothing changes. The questions of Unpoly and Turbo stay theirs.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;dialog data-partial-confirm-dialog aria-labelledby="confirm-question"&gt;
    &lt;p id="confirm-question" data-partial-confirm-question&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button type="button" value="cancel" autofocus&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button type="button" value="confirm"&gt;Confirm&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/dialog&gt;</code></pre>
</article>


